debug.log

# NOTE: this file previously listed ".gitignore" itself. That meant the file was never
# committed, so none of the exclusions below would reach a clone. Given Dev/ holds real
# customer configuration exports, an uncommitted .gitignore is a disclosure risk, so the
# self-exclusion has been removed deliberately.

### PowerShell ###
# Exclude packaged modules
*.zip

# Exclude .NET assemblies from source
*.dll

### vscode ###
.vscode/tasks.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/extensions.json
*.code-workspace

### copilot ###
# Ignore the whole folder recursively. The previous pattern .copilot/*.* only matched files
# directly inside .copilot, because a single asterisk does not cross a directory separator.
# That left .copilot/output (generated reports and the saved AsBuilt config) tracked.
.copilot/

### development ###
# Dev/ is published so contributors get the diagnostic and regression harnesses. It also
# holds real customer configuration exports during development, so the exclusions below are
# a safety boundary rather than housekeeping. Read them before adding anything to Dev.
#
# The rule is deny by default: every configuration export format is ignored wherever it
# appears, and the sample folders are ignored outright. Publishing a sanitised sample is a
# deliberate act requiring "git add -f", which is the intended friction.

# Any configuration export, anywhere in the tree, whatever it is named.
*.tar
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
symphonyconfig.xml

# Sample folders are ignored wholesale, so a newly created one is never tracked by accident.
Dev/Private Samples/
Dev/More Samples/
Dev/Samples/

# Documentation about the samples is safe to publish and is not caught by the rules above.
# The configuration exports themselves stay blocked by the format rules at the top of this
# section regardless of which folder they are in.
!Dev/Samples/
Dev/Samples/*
!Dev/Samples/*.md

# Generated report output from the harnesses.
Dev/output/


# Word and PDF exports, which may be rendered from a real configuration.
*.docx
*.pdf
Tests/coverage.xml

